Z||000011||firstfiero||03-20-2001||07:59 PM||||      Came with some plastic strips also. Two of them I put in the wind deflector in the middle. Where the hell do the other two go? And why the hell does the whole bra lift up when I turn my head lights on? I can't quite get it stretched far enough to keep it completly out of the way.   ||||reg||6
Z||000012||stsmithgt||03-21-2001||10:06 AM||||All the plastic strips go in those slots to make a wind deflector.  There's a slot for all of them. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">  DOH! I forgot to make bra pics.  For the lifting of the bra, you are suppose to pull open the velcro covers on the lights, roll them up, and use those little velcro straps to retain them above the headlight covers.  <BR>     If it still lifts up, you need to pull the cover higher up the hood.  It's a tight fit and best installed while the bra is warm, like on a warm day to make it more plyable.  Being new and cold, I can imagine it being a PITA. <BR>     I shoe horned those upper plastic covered hooks between the fender and fender well.  It allows me to put a sharper curve in the hook for a stronger hold to keep it tight.  That eliminates a lot of hang up problems.||||reg||1
Z||000013||firstfiero||03-21-2001||10:24 AM||||     Thanks...I know about rolling up the covers...I not a complete idiot....just a partial   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> anyway thats what I figured. Putting a bra on a car is like putting felt on a pool table. Every time you think you have it tight it relaxes again...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  by the way it seems like I can still get under the hood pretty easy...just un hook those to rubber ended hooks..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"> I take my sunroof out alot in the summer so I was afraid it would be a big hassle.   ||||reg||14
Z||000014||firstfiero||03-21-2001||10:24 AM||||     Thanks...I know about rolling up the covers...I not a complete idiot....just a partial   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> anyway thats what I figured. Putting a bra on a car is like putting felt on a pool table. Every time you think you have it tight it relaxes again...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  by the way it seems like I can still get under the hood pretty easy...just un hook those to rubber ended hooks..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"> I take my sunroof out alot in the summer so I was afraid it would be a big hassle.   ||||reg||14
Z||000015||stsmithgt||03-21-2001||11:09 AM||||When I first got mine, I thought the same thing because my sun roof is off as much as possible.  The bottom felt hooks in the fender well tend to slide out a little when lifting the hood up to the first latch.  It's fairly easy to re-hook the rubber covered ones and slide the felt covered ones back into place AND LET THE SUN SHINE IN WITH THE ROOF OFF! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000016||firstfiero||03-21-2001||01:08 PM||||   HELL YA!! Couldn't be any better unless you have a t-top...That's a far of dream of an upgrade.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000017||stsmithgt||03-22-2001||10:47 AM||||Ok, I finally got around to taking some pics.  I suppose their might be some curious folks out their wondering why we're talking about "bras". Three simple pics showing the straps, straps hooked, and what it looks like from the other side, which shows the air deflector where those four plastic pieces slide in.  I hope the sun comes out today. It's darker then what the photos look like. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/brastrap1a.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/brastrap2a.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/brastrap3a.jpg">  <BR>It was in the low 60's so I put it all the way on, but need to snug it up when it warms up.  It was about six o'clock this mourning when I took these at work.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 03-22-2001).]||||reg||1
